  ("How much final expense coverage does a California family need?", "An immediate burial at California&rsquo;s $2,499 median plus $2,000&ndash;$5,000 of cemetery costs is $4,499&ndash;$7,499, and a full traditional funeral with a viewing and cemetery costs comes to $8,415&ndash;$11,415. In the coastal metros the cemetery can push those totals higher, so $15,000 is a reasonable target for burial; $10,000 covers cremation with a memorial."),
  ("How reliable are these California figures?", "More reliable than for any other state in our data: 90 price lists, against 13 for North Carolina and 24 for Pennsylvania. A median drawn from 90 funeral homes across a state of 58 counties is a genuine benchmark. The number it cannot include is your cemetery&rsquo;s plot price, which is where California varies most."),
  ("Who regulates final expense insurance in California?", "The California Department of Insurance, which licenses agents and carriers, has a &ldquo;Check License Status&rdquo; tool on its homepage, and publishes a consumer complaint study comparing insurers. Ask your agent for their California license number."),
